  "definition": "A child not enrolled in public or private school, as the Pulse files define it (TENROLLHMSCH). The Pulse level (14.4 percent) is not read; the state share is the NHES national share, 0.028, times how far the state's Pulse share sits from the nation's, shrunk toward the nation by 40 households: state share = 0.028 x (n x state_pulse_share + 40 x national_pulse_share) / ((n + 40) x national_pulse_share).",
  "limits": "State samples are small (25 to 263 household records); the relative pattern is from 2022 and the NHES anchor is 2019. The share calibrates the band a played town's schools report and never picks which family homeschools. A state the file lacks (the five territories) takes the median, marked ESTIMATED.",
